Interpretation: folding K into a generating-function marker x removes
K's own symbolic-degree-binomial obstruction cleanly, but the SAME
kind of obstruction reappears on r once r is also left symbolic. The
obstruction is not specifically 'about K' -- it is about having TWO
simultaneous free 'family-size' parameters (K and r) each entering a
binomial coefficient's DEGREE while also coupling to the summation
variable. This is a sharper structural diagnosis than either Estagio
39's or Estagio 44's own (each of which only ever had ONE such
parameter -- K alone -- left symbolic at the point of certification).
